@meta title="My CLI Tool" license=MIT lang=rust

@h1 widget [#widget]
@p `widget` is a small CLI for transforming widget configurations. It reads
@p JSON from stdin, applies a transformation, and writes the result to stdout.

@h2 Install [#install]
@code lang=shell
~~~
cargo install widget
~~~

@h2 Quick start [#quickstart]
@p Pipe a config through and inspect the output.

@code lang=shell
~~~
echo '{"size": 4}' | widget --multiply 3
# => {"size": 12}
~~~

@h2 Commands [#commands]
@ul
- `widget --multiply N` — multiply every numeric leaf by N
- `widget --filter KEY` — keep only the named keys
- `widget --schema` — print the JSON schema and exit
- `widget --version` — print the version

@h2 Configuration [#config]
@p Configuration is read from `~/.widgetrc.toml` if present.

@code lang=toml
~~~
default_multiplier = 1
strict = true
allow_unknown_keys = false
~~~

@h2 Contributing [#contributing]
@ol
- fork and clone the repo
- run `cargo test` before pushing
- open a PR against `main`; CI must be green

@h2 License [#license]
@p MIT — see the LICENSE file in the repository root.
